WEBVTT

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.500
<i>(After many years have lapsed)</i>

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:39.280
I'm alive. No injury, nothing. Why?

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.650
It's a waste of time
trying to escape from here.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:11.650
This place is a natural fortress that
nobody can access or get out of.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.650
Answer me. Why don't you kill me?

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:27.000
I ask you back.
How valuable is your existence to him?

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.620
He killed my sister.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.170
He is the man who murdered
his wife with his own hands.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.170
Would it put him into a living hell
to lose you, or not?

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.680
Until I find it out, I will let you live.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.310
That's the reason why I brought you here.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.020
If you're the most important person to him,

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.190
he'll find this place and come here soon.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:52.690
Then, I'll kill you in front of him,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.320
and make him feel the same as I have.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.650
After that,
I'll torture and kill him slowly.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.070
However...

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.490
If he doesn't show up,
I have nothing to do with you.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:07.540
I will let you go home alive,
so for a while, stay here and be quiet.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:20.510
I wonder how valuable I am to Kenshin?

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.740
<i>Tomoe has continued to exist</i>
<i>at the bottom of Kenshin's heart</i>

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.820
<i>with the cross-shaped scar,</i>

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:49.000
<i>a deep, sad existence which</i>
<i>won't disappear until he dies.</i>

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.670
<i>She gained her place in his heart</i>
<i>in exchange for her life.</i>

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.760
<i>How can I do as she did?</i>
<i>I have no idea.</i>

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.590
<i>I envy Tomoe.</i>

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:09.980
<i>If I die, will you</i>
<i>remember me forever, Kenshin?</i>

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.620
I swore I'd punish the person
who once was called

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.040
the strongest assassin
in the last days of the Tokugawa.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.210
I can match him in swordsmanship.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.960
I've thoroughly investigated
the Hiten sword technique,

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.760
including its secrets.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:44.130
I don't need any help.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:49.220
I will punish him myself, with my own hands.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.160
<i>I wonder whether Kenshin,</i>
<i>tormented by his guilt,</i>

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.990
<i>will lose against this person</i>
<i>who is willing to punish him?</i>

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.610
Sister...

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.700
Sister...

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.330
Why?

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.160
Why did you die?!

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.540
Sister...

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.710
<i>He's also so lonely.</i>

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:09.390
<i>I'm sure that he's lived alone</i>
<i>with his grudge and hate.</i>

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.390
What the hell is this?

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.900
I'm a woman, so of course I can cook.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.980
It's no different making breakfast for one,
or for two, so I made extra.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.740
I don't care if you eat or not.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.530
Sister...

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.770
You are waiting for him, aren't you?

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:28.030
If he comes, I'll kill you, but even so,
you're hoping he'll come?

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.860
Sometimes, people feel more pain
living than dying.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.830
That's what you told me, a "living hell."

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:41.370
For me, a "living hell" means losing Kenshin.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:47.130
I don't know if he really needs me or not.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:51.470
However, I hope so,
I want to believe so. That's why...

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.510
He took many people's lives and happiness

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.300
away from them, erased them
with his own hands.

00:07:57.430 --> 00:08:01.680
The people left behind are still
in the darkness of sadness and desperation.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:04.980
His guilt is unfathomably great and deep.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:10.480
Even so, he hasn't been judged and
lives peacefully in the Meiji era.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:15.530
Why? How can he live?!
Why do you love a person like him?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.080
He doesn't have any right to be happy.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.990
He should never receive love from anyone!

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.540
Kenshin loved Tomoe.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:27.670
That's why he's been suffering over it,
even now.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:31.760
He has a burden;
he killed the person he loved.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:37.430
He has been accusing himself
and he can't forgive himself.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:41.180
But he had to stay alive,

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:43.600
because that's what Tomoe wanted him to do.

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:49.020
Your sister, she forgave Kenshin,
who killed her fiance.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.780
I understand how she felt,

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:56.570
because I'm a woman who loves
the same person she did.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:01.240
He's been living by saving
more people than he killed,

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:04.710
and he has been seeking for a way
to atone for his guilt.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.040
The answer of atonement...

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.160
You said he's been seeking
for a way of atonement.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.670
I think it's time to give him an answer.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.670
Get ready.
We will go to the seashoreand wait for him.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:00.470
For me, it took fifteen years to walk
through this route of revenge.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:05.020
Even if my sister forgave him,
I can't. Never.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:08.690
The answer is to punish him
with my own hands!

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:25.450
Kenshin!

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.330
I won't give this woman to you.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.790
If you want to get her back,
you'll have to fight me.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.500
I will kill him by myself.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:36.550
If you want to go to him, you'll have to
commit suicide and follow him.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:41.300
Miss Kaoru, don't worry.
Please wait there.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:21.930
<i>Kenshin is different from just a while ago.</i>

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.720
<i>His sword doesn't show</i>
<i>any hesitation or confusion,</i>

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:28.720
<i>and I feel he's stronger than before.</i>

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:32.690
<i>I wonder if Kenshin finally found</i>
<i>the answer he had been seeking so long?</i>

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.690
You make me laugh
if you're thinking about not killing me.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:41.450
You are also disqualified
to be an assassin.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.620
The guilt of murder can be atoned
only by your death,

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.080
however, the dead don't have
any way to punish you.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:59.130
So, those who loved the dead person
must execute it as their successor.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:01.920
That's what "Jinchu" means.
You're a criminal.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.050
Scream, suffer the pain! Regret!

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:07.140
Regret what you did to my sister,
taking away her happiness!

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:11.310
You made my life crazy and smashed it.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:19.980
Die with the grief, anger, and vengeance
of those left behind carved into your body.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:36.670
I'm not afraid of dying.
However, my life is not only mine.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:40.670
The women who died for me
when I was little,

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:43.130
and Tomoe... I was made to live by them.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:47.090
In order to light more smiles
and happiness in this world,

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:52.520
as long as I live, I risk my sword and
my mind for those who are alive now,

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.190
and I will complete my life.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.770
This is the answer I found as
a way of atonement, led by Tomoe's smile.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:02.280
<i>Kenshin...</i>

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:07.320
What I wanted was
happiness for my only sister,

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.280
above that of all the people in this world.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:15.290
But you ruined it, stepped on it,
and erased it along with her life.

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.960
I don't have anybody to protect now.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:21.960
What's left for me is
only the flames and fire of anger.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.300
That's why I'm going to kill you.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:26.970
My hand started the flame of fire in you,

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:32.220
and if anger is the only truth for you,

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:35.310
then at least I have to face it.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.390
Enishi, I am so sorry.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:23.610
I don't think my guilt will be
forgiven even if I win.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.940
No matter what answer I come up with,

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:30.110
I know your vengeance and sadness
will not disappear.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:35.120
However, if your smile will come back
to you in exchange for my life...

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:38.960
You are telling me that
you will accept the punishment, aren't you?

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.620
Then at once!

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:59.100
Sister, are you telling me
not to take revenge?

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:03.480
Do I need to forgive someone like him?

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:10.110
Sister... How frustrating!

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.820
If he had never existed...

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.950
Damn... Damn... Sister...

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:29.800
<i>Your answer, your life of battle,</i>
<i>I will watch it until the end.</i>

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:34.430
<i>That's what Enishi Yukishiro said</i>
<i>when he left.</i>

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:39.520
<i>No matter how much heart you put into it,</i>

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.140
<i>atonement can't be achieved without</i>
<i>the other person's forgiveness.</i>

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:47.480
<i>You might never be forgiven, but...</i>

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:52.450
Miss Kaoru, let's go home together.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.700
<i>Even so he smiles at me.</i>

00:15:56.870 --> 00:16:01.200
<i>His usual smile that secretly hides</i>
<i>his sadness behind his gentleness.</i>

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:04.170
<i>I want to reply to this smile.</i>

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:07.170
<i>I can't exchange my life and his,</i>

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:10.010
<i>but at least I'd like to be at</i>
<i>his side and support him</i>

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:14.880
<i>until the day when he smiles at me</i>
<i>from the bottom of his heart.</i>

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.720
<i>That's my true answer.</i>

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:24.190
<i>It's ordinary and nothing special,</i>
<i>but it's the most important.</i>

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.740
<i>Miss Tomoe...</i>

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:39.080
<i>I might not be able to live a life of</i>
<i>integrity and rigor like you did.</i>

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:44.410
<i>I don't think I can be more important</i>
<i>than you were for Kenshin.</i>

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:51.670
<i>However, I will support him</i>
<i>as much as I can, in the best way I can.</i>

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:54.880
<i>So, please.</i>

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.430
<i>Please entrust Kenshin to me.</i>

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.430
<i>Miss Tomoe...</i>

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:12.190
How are you feeling, Kaoru?

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.440
Sorry, Yahiko, I'm being a bother.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:18.740
It's nothing.
The doctor said you need rest.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.950
I can take care of you at a time like this,
so don't overdo anything.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:24.700
I've been dreaming.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:29.080
About the days after I met Kenshin,
up to the days we were married.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.630
Old story.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:35.420
Yes, but I feel like
it was just a short while ago.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:40.050
After the world calmed down
and everyone went their own way,

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:43.180
starting the journey for their own lives.

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:47.390
I left here too. So things have
happened which I don't know about,

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.980
but it must have been hard for you
to live here after that.

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:55.990
Even after he got the answer,
he lived in battles more than before.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:18:00.740
He told me he would do as much as he could
while he was able to use his sword.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.740
His thoughts are left to you
along with his reversed blade sword.

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:07.750
Passed on to you, Yahiko.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:14.630
That was a good one. Can you stand up?

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:15.840
Yes...

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:21.300
Yahiko, this is a gift
for your coming-of-age ritual. Take it.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:30.940
Miss Megumi told me about it,
so I was prepared.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:35.110
So many battles and scars...
the rebounds of Mitsurugi swordsmanship

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:41.450
they undermine his small body
so his life as a swordsman won't be much longer.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.540
Kaoru...

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.040
Yes...

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:54.790
I've been thinking ever
since I left my sword.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:59.840
Times are becoming peaceful, however,
unhappiness never disappears.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:04.550
The scars of wars, natural disasters,
illnesses and poverty...

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:08.810
I think these won't disappear
no matter how times change.

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:12.730
However, if there is anything I can do...

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:18.360
I no longer have a sword and
I've lost the power to protect people.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:20.990
What I can do now isn't reach out
to help from above;

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:23.320
it's share their pain and suffering,

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:26.330
and do my meager best
to encourage them to live on.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:29.660
Kaoru, would you allow me to do so?

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.670
That's what you chose.

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:38.760
Please be confident and go your own way.

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:44.430
I have already received more than
enough happiness from you.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.720
I will wait for you.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.430
In order to welcome you with a smile.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.650
No matter when you come back,
I will wait for you with our child.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.780
Then he traveled all over Japan?

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:02.150
But he always came back.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:06.870
And while he was here, he kept smiling,

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:10.950
but his smile contained deep sadness.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:16.420
Natural disaster or epidemics
take human lives mercilessly.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:21.090
No matter how well you take care
of your patients, they die.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:26.720
The reality of being shunned and hated
just for having fallen ill.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:30.270
People were depressed and fought
against desperation day by day.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:34.390
The only thing I can do is
to raise this child safely,

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:37.480
and let him leave the house
with a smile.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.110
I feel it's been a very long time,
or sometimes,

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.980
it's seemed a short time
for fifteen years.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:43.440
Kenji grew and has left me now.

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:48.490
The only thing left for me is
to wait for him to come back.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:54.160
That's why I asked him to share
a little piece of his suffering.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:59.170
I wanted to have something
which we could share,

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:02.170
because we are husband and wife.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:10.350
Kaoru...

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:11.930
Yes?

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.480
Thank you.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:21.190
I've been able to live the way
I chose because of you.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:25.820
I have no words to express my appreciation.
Thank you very much.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:31.160
But to you and Kenji,
I apologize from the bottom of my heart,

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:34.540
because I was not a good husband and father.

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.460
I am so sorry to have made you
suffer through painful days...

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:44.960
I've found out how happy it is to devote
yourself to someone when I met you.

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:49.640
If I'm successful in supporting you...

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:55.520
if you think so, then
there is no greater happiness.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:00.230
I'm happy.
I've been happy and I will be forever.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:04.150
So please, come home.

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:07.990
Please don't leave me alone.

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:45.190
Please share your pain with me.

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:48.280
If I have it,
I know I can suffer without you,

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:51.740
because I am your wife.

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:54.450
I'm sorry.

00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.710
Kaoru...

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:24.980
Kenshin...

00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:28.480
The name Kenshin was given by my teacher,

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:30.900
to fit a man living by the sword.

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:35.490
Now my life with the sword has ended,
it's not fit for me any longer.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:39.000
My parents named me Shinta.

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:40.830
That's my real name.

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:43.500
Shinta...

00:23:44.750 --> 00:23:47.340
When I come back,

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:50.170
can you call me by that name?

00:24:41.100 --> 00:24:43.560
Kenshin!

00:25:07.540 --> 00:25:08.590
Kenshin!

00:25:13.420 --> 00:25:15.010
kenshin...?

00:25:15.130 --> 00:25:17.720
Kenshin, are you...

00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:20.600
I have to go home.

00:25:23.310 --> 00:25:25.270
I'm going to bring a doctor.

00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:27.270
Wait here, Kenshin!

00:26:24.490 --> 00:26:27.080
Miss. Megumi, long time no see.

00:26:27.660 --> 00:26:29.120
You came all the way here from Aizu?

00:26:29.250 --> 00:26:34.090
Of course! I was asked by Kenshin
to take care of you.

00:26:34.210 --> 00:26:36.090
Well, let me see.

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:44.850
Kenshin... Sanosuke...

00:26:45.600 --> 00:26:47.680
You don't need to force yourself
to remember things.

00:26:47.850 --> 00:26:51.480
Rather, the first priority is
to recover your health.

00:26:51.600 --> 00:26:53.310
It's done now. Eat!

00:27:41.780 --> 00:27:43.240
Isn't it good?

00:27:45.830 --> 00:27:47.080
Yes.

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:54.500
There is nothing left for you
to do in this country.

00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:57.880
I will make you go back to Japan.

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:00.210
To the place where Kaoru is.

00:28:00.340 --> 00:28:02.090
Kaoru...

00:28:06.140 --> 00:28:09.100
I don't think I will be able
to go back to Aizu soon.

00:28:09.520 --> 00:28:12.100
I will stay here for a while. Is it okay?

00:28:12.690 --> 00:28:14.350
Oh, yes, but...

00:28:14.690 --> 00:28:16.270
I told you.

00:28:16.440 --> 00:28:18.940
Kenshin asked me to take care of you.

00:28:19.110 --> 00:28:22.110
I have a responsibility as a doctor.

00:28:22.700 --> 00:28:24.240
I'm sorry.

00:28:26.370 --> 00:28:27.620
Wind chimes?

00:28:28.330 --> 00:28:31.750
It was summer when Kenshin left here.

00:28:31.870 --> 00:28:33.620
So I keep it just as it was.

00:28:39.800 --> 00:28:43.470
Then you have to be fine
until he comes home, right?

00:28:50.220 --> 00:28:51.970
Where is Yahiko?

00:28:52.140 --> 00:28:53.480
He went to Kyoto.

00:28:54.230 --> 00:28:56.560
He told me he'd bring Kenji back.

00:28:56.690 --> 00:28:57.900
I see.

00:28:58.020 --> 00:29:01.230
Ms. Megumi, how is Ms. Kaoru?

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:03.690
Yes, it's the same disease as Kenshin.

00:29:04.070 --> 00:29:06.450
A serious disease which
we don't have any idea how to cure.

00:29:06.570 --> 00:29:08.910
and worse than that, there's
no medicine that will stop its progress.

00:29:09.030 --> 00:29:10.080
Oh, no!

00:29:10.200 --> 00:29:13.500
She accepted a disease
like that intentionally.

00:29:20.710 --> 00:29:24.970
But that's so sad.

00:29:25.090 --> 00:29:28.010
That's her way to show her devotion.

00:29:28.180 --> 00:29:31.640
I believe she didn't hesitate to do it,
nor does she regret it.

00:29:31.760 --> 00:29:35.600
Indeed, it's her way. I mean
she wasn't in a negative attitude.

00:29:35.730 --> 00:29:39.480
She turns pain into a bond,
and hardship into hope,

00:29:39.610 --> 00:29:42.020
while waiting for the person
she loves to return.

00:29:42.190 --> 00:29:44.190
That's why I can't give up on her either.

00:29:44.360 --> 00:29:48.490
I can't lose the battle,
as a doctor and as a woman.

00:29:58.870 --> 00:30:01.130
<i>In order to get onto a ship to Japan,</i>

00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:03.960
<i>we will probably have to go to Shanghai.</i>

00:30:07.550 --> 00:30:12.350
<i>But I don't think he can survive</i>
<i>a long voyage in his condition.</i>

00:30:12.470 --> 00:30:13.890
<i>What shall I do?</i>

00:30:45.090 --> 00:30:50.630
I don't want to kill animals,
but for my friend, I have to have your liver.

00:30:50.760 --> 00:30:51.680
Sorry.

00:30:59.600 --> 00:31:00.600
Kenji...

00:31:03.650 --> 00:31:05.270
Mr. Yahiko?

00:31:06.780 --> 00:31:08.740
I can't go home yet.

00:31:08.860 --> 00:31:10.280
Kenji!

00:31:10.700 --> 00:31:15.700
The person my mother has been
waiting for isn't me.

00:31:15.830 --> 00:31:18.580
I haven't found out
what true strength is yet.

00:31:18.700 --> 00:31:21.210
Until I see the answer
with my own eyes, I...

00:31:21.330 --> 00:31:23.290
True strength?

00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:28.130
Why don't you ask this sword about it?

00:31:28.880 --> 00:31:31.760
That is the reversed blade sword.

00:31:31.880 --> 00:31:34.140
You keep it for one night.

00:31:34.720 --> 00:31:39.100
If you can't understand,
then I will teach you myself.

00:31:49.990 --> 00:31:51.780
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:31:51.900 --> 00:31:54.490
I'm going to make
a special meat dish for you tonight.

00:32:04.210 --> 00:32:06.250
<i>Is there any meaning to this sword</i>

00:32:06.380 --> 00:32:09.300
<i>that my father kept</i>
<i>after he quit being an assassin?</i>

00:32:09.420 --> 00:32:11.840
<i>He was strong and became a legend,</i>

00:32:12.010 --> 00:32:13.680
<i>but it was in the last days of the Tokugawa.</i>

00:32:13.840 --> 00:32:18.510
<i>The father I knew was not even</i>
<i>a man who lived by the sword.</i>

00:32:19.350 --> 00:32:24.310
<i>He didn't carry the sword</i>
<i>and didn't come home for long periods.</i>

00:32:24.440 --> 00:32:27.520
<i>My mother was always waiting for him.</i>

00:32:28.690 --> 00:32:31.280
<i>What I wanted to be passed on</i>
<i>was not the Kasshin swordsmanship,</i>

00:32:31.400 --> 00:32:33.320
<i>nor my father's sword</i>
<i>which doesn't kill people,</i>

00:32:33.450 --> 00:32:35.530
<i>but Hiten Mitsurugi swordsmanship.</i>

00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:41.540
<i>I will learn it and create</i>
<i>a new legend superior to my father's.</i>

00:32:58.890 --> 00:33:00.180
I am sorry.

00:33:00.310 --> 00:33:02.980
I came here without telling you
and carried on with my business.

00:33:03.100 --> 00:33:05.480
You don't need to worry about it.

00:33:07.400 --> 00:33:10.980
First of all, I don't intend to give
my swordsmanship to anybody.

00:33:11.110 --> 00:33:14.740
Mitsurugi swordsmanship will die with me.

00:33:18.070 --> 00:33:19.910
Once you have a power,

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:22.660
sometimes you are put in a situation
which makes you carry extra burdens,

00:33:22.790 --> 00:33:25.250
and live all your life with pain.

00:33:25.410 --> 00:33:28.000
Just like me... and him.

00:33:28.830 --> 00:33:31.710
The secret of
Mitsurugi swordsmanship is

00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:33.760
to protect the weak
from pain in troubled times.

00:33:33.920 --> 00:33:38.180
However, the times have changed dramatically,
and it's become a relic of the past.

00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:41.430
Everything is destined
to change and disappear.

00:33:41.560 --> 00:33:45.100
Only the moon remains unchanged.

00:34:24.310 --> 00:34:25.310
Good morning.

00:34:33.150 --> 00:34:36.320
This is an herb medicine which
mainly contains ginseng.

00:34:36.490 --> 00:34:39.320
Its effects will help
your constitution and warm your body.

00:34:39.490 --> 00:34:41.280
It's bitter and horrible.

00:34:41.410 --> 00:34:42.490
Don't complain.

00:34:43.080 --> 00:34:44.290
I'm sorry.

00:34:44.410 --> 00:34:45.950
You...

00:34:46.080 --> 00:34:48.750
You can smile like that
in any condition, can't you?

00:34:48.870 --> 00:34:51.420
Because you told me, Ms. Megumi.

00:34:51.710 --> 00:34:56.000
The most effective medicine for
Kenshin's cross-shaped scar is my smile.

00:34:56.170 --> 00:35:00.300
That's why I try to smile any time,
in any condition.

00:35:00.430 --> 00:35:03.010
So it's become a habit now.

00:35:03.680 --> 00:35:06.680
<i>The reason why Kenshin chose you...</i>

00:35:06.850 --> 00:35:08.770
<i>I really understand.</i>

00:35:47.390 --> 00:35:51.770
<i>Indeed you are a genius at swordsmanship.</i>
<i>I almost envy you, Kenji.</i>

00:35:51.890 --> 00:35:57.020
<i>However, I know you already realize that</i>
<i>you can't be superior to Kenshinwith talent alone.</i>

00:35:57.150 --> 00:36:02.070
<i>In the next attack, I'm going to include all of</i>
<i>the feelings I've felt throughout my battles.</i>

00:36:02.450 --> 00:36:04.490
<i>Just like me at that time.</i>

00:36:04.620 --> 00:36:08.580
<i>Accept it and feel the strength of</i>
<i>Kenshin's mind, sealed in this sword.</i>

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.590
<i>Heavy...</i>

00:36:23.630 --> 00:36:26.850
It's a little late, but this is a gift
for your coming-of-age ritual.

00:36:26.970 --> 00:36:29.350
Accept it officially now, Kenji.

00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:43.240
<i>My idiot student thinks he's changed</i>
<i>the secret of swordsmanship.</i>

00:36:46.780 --> 00:36:49.950
Shanghai is close. Don't let
the horse shake you off, Kenshin!

00:37:02.130 --> 00:37:03.470
Kenshin!

00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:09.760
Kenshin, the cargo ship will
take you to Yokohama.

00:37:09.890 --> 00:37:13.270
When you go back to Japan,
when you see Kaoru...

00:37:13.390 --> 00:37:16.270
I'm sure your memory will come back at once.

00:37:16.400 --> 00:37:18.480
I've already asked someone to help you.

00:37:18.650 --> 00:37:23.070
I really want to take you home by myself,
but I have things to do here.

00:37:23.820 --> 00:37:25.740
I have to say goodbye.

00:37:27.160 --> 00:37:29.450
Sanosuke...

00:37:29.740 --> 00:37:31.950
Thank you.

00:37:35.750 --> 00:37:38.080
<i>I'm the one to say thank you, not you.</i>

00:37:38.210 --> 00:37:41.630
<i>You have changed me and changed everybody.</i>

00:37:41.750 --> 00:37:46.510
<i>I will live as I am, just like you did.</i>

00:37:47.090 --> 00:37:49.220
<i>Goodbye, Kenshin.</i>

00:37:57.600 --> 00:37:59.020
Kenji...

00:38:00.360 --> 00:38:01.360
I'm home.

00:38:02.690 --> 00:38:04.990
I am sorry, I...

00:38:05.110 --> 00:38:08.160
Don't say sorry to a son
who ran away from home.

00:38:09.240 --> 00:38:10.370
Kenji.

00:38:11.030 --> 00:38:12.660
The cherry trees are blooming.

00:38:12.780 --> 00:38:15.870
Let's go see the cherry blossoms
like we do every year. So...

00:38:18.120 --> 00:38:19.620
Yes...

00:38:44.610 --> 00:38:45.900
Kaoru...

00:40:06.150 --> 00:40:07.650
Kaoru...

00:41:00.410 --> 00:41:02.830
I am home...

00:41:03.410 --> 00:41:05.210
Kaoru...

00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:10.630
Welcome home... Shinta...

00:41:15.630 --> 00:41:19.890
I wonder how long
the cherry blossoms will last?

00:41:21.140 --> 00:41:25.310
Kenji, Yahiko, Tsubame and
Ms. Megumi, and Ms. Tae...

00:41:25.440 --> 00:41:29.060
I want to go to a cherry blossom viewing
and invite everybody.

00:41:29.230 --> 00:41:33.360
And next year, and the year after next.

00:41:34.490 --> 00:41:37.860
Then Yahiko might be a father.

00:41:39.780 --> 00:41:41.240
Shinta?

00:41:42.740 --> 00:41:44.450
You're tired, aren't you?

00:42:01.010 --> 00:42:02.600
Finally...

00:42:03.890 --> 00:42:06.430
It's finally disappeared.

00:42:35.550 --> 00:42:38.930
<i>Don't worry. I know he'll be back.</i>

00:42:39.050 --> 00:42:43.470
<i>As you know, he comes back every time,</i>
<i>no matter what happens.</i>

00:42:46.640 --> 00:42:54.900
<i>Recalling our past, both you and I</i>
<i>have lived with scars which won't fade.</i>

00:42:55.480 --> 00:42:58.780
<i>Scars which were carved as a cross.</i>

00:43:02.030 --> 00:43:03.910
<i>I wonder if I can do it...</i>

00:43:04.030 --> 00:43:09.410
<i>If I can share</i>
<i>his pain and the weight of his sword.</i>

00:43:13.080 --> 00:43:15.800
<i>Cherry blossoms are beautiful</i>
<i>while they are out,</i>

00:43:15.920 --> 00:43:18.090
<i>but it's also beautiful when they're falling.</i>

00:43:18.210 --> 00:43:22.840
<i>You don't need to force yourself</i>
<i>to smile in front of me.</i>

00:43:26.180 --> 00:43:28.310
<i>Yes, matters of the past are</i>
<i>the same as dreams,</i>

00:43:28.430 --> 00:43:32.810
<i>and they will fade in time</i>
<i>and disappear someday.</i>

00:43:36.940 --> 00:43:41.700
<i>Someday, he will show me his smile</i>
<i>from the bottom of his heart.</i>

00:43:41.860 --> 00:43:44.120
<i>I believe so.</i>

00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:55.670
<i>I knew that the times need him</i>
<i>and I couldn't change his way of life.</i>

00:43:57.050 --> 00:43:59.010
<i>I know that.</i>

00:43:59.590 --> 00:44:02.880
<i>I knew that, but...</i>

00:44:09.970 --> 00:44:14.150
<i>Thank you so very much</i>
<i>for everything until now.</i>

00:44:16.480 --> 00:44:20.530
<i>Goodbye... Kaoru...</i>

00:45:00.110 --> 00:45:03.740
Kenji, what's wrong?

00:45:03.860 --> 00:45:05.860
Oh, nothing.

00:45:11.870 --> 00:45:13.410
What is it?

00:45:13.540 --> 00:45:16.080
I'll tell you later.

00:45:16.210 --> 00:45:19.250
Anyway, Chizuru,
that ribbon looks good on you.

00:45:19.380 --> 00:45:20.750
Really?

00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:25.050
We'll live happily. Won't we?

00:45:25.180 --> 00:45:26.590
Yes!
